  "nl_text": "The rschema_0322 database is designed to manage information about companies, employees, devices, users, and their interactions. The database contains seven tables: company, employee, device, user, site, employee_uses_device, and user_creates_site. The company table stores details about each company, including its unique identifier, name, website, and creation date. The employee table contains information about each employee, such as their unique identifier, name, position, salary, and the company they belong to, with the company ID referencing the company table and enforcing a cascade delete and update rule. The device table stores details about each device, including its unique identifier, name, and the employee it belongs to, with the employee ID referencing the employee table and enforcing a cascade delete and update rule. The user table stores user credentials, including their unique identifier, username, password, email, and last login time. The site table contains information about each site, including its name, hostname, status, and the user who created it, with the user ID referencing the user table and enforcing a cascade delete and update rule. The employee_uses_device table tracks the usage of devices by employees, including the employee ID, device ID, start and end usage times, and forms a composite primary key with these three columns. This table also references the employee and device tables, enforcing a cascade delete and update rule. Finally, the user_creates_site table stores information about which user created each site, including the username, site name, and creation time, with a composite primary key and referencing the user and site tables, enforcing a cascade delete and update rule.",
  "gold_question": "The enterprise management system is required to manage information regarding companies, users, employees, devices, and sites simultaneously. In the system, each company shall be recorded with its name, website address, and creation time. A company may have multiple employees; their names, positions, and salaries are to be stored and associated with their respective companies. Each employee may use multiple devices; the system shall record the name of each device and specify the employee to whom it belongs. Regarding user information, the system shall store usernames, emails, passwords, and the last login time, and link users to the sites they have created. Each site shall have a unique name and hostname and can be marked as deleted.",
  "input_json": "/data/RSchema_ExpResults4/Experiment2/schema2text_llama31/0322.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0322\nCREATE TABLE `company` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `website` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `creation_date` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `employee` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `position` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `salary` decimal(10,2) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `company_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `employee_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`company_id`) REFERENCES `company` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `device` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `employee_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `device_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`employee_id`) REFERENCES `employee` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `user` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `username` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `password` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `email` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `last_login` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `site` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `hostname` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `status` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `site_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `user` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `employee_uses_device` (\n  `employee_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `device_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `start_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `end_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`employee_id`, `device_id`, `start_time`),\n  CONSTRAINT `employee_uses_device_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`employee_id`) REFERENCES `employee` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `employee_uses_device_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`device_id`) REFERENCES `device` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `user_creates_site` (\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `site_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `creation_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`user_id`, `site_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `user_creates_site_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `user` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `user_creates_site_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`site_id`) REFERENCES `site` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
